A Zentrale courier reaches Hoelz near Hettstedt with money and a cart of rifles. For a few days his bands and the miners' fighting groups act together, and they hold the roads.

@discipline
subtitle: The Right's way. Slower, but the fighters will answer to someone.
on-arrival: e21_ma_hoelz = 2; crisis_momentum += 3; red_guards_loyalty += 5; unionist_satisfaction += 3; lean_unionist += 1

Hoelz agrees to coordinate with the strike committees, more or less. He keeps his dynamite.

@disown
subtitle: The Spartacist line. The strike stays clean; it may also stay weaker.
on-arrival: e21_ma_hoelz = 3; crisis_momentum -= 3; spd_relation += 3; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5; offensive_satisfaction -= 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1

The Rote Fahne declares that bank robbery is not a communist tactic. Hoelz reads it, laughs, and carries on.
